# Mobile figures

Seven figures, 60 mm tall, each with a flat back, a 1.6 mm edge band and a rounded front rising 3.2 mm. Every figure has a 2.0 mm hole for the thread, placed above its centre of gravity with at least 2.5 mm of material around it, so it hangs straight.

## Printing

Import at 100% scale in millimetres. Print flat back down, no supports, with a brim if the figure is slim. About 0.2 mm layers and enough walls to fill the edge band work well; use fine or adaptive layers for the gently curved crown. Print each figure in its own colour, or pause for a colour change at the top of the edge band.

## Hanging

Thread a cord through the hole from front to back and tie a loop, or knot the cord through the hole directly. Hang the figures from the mobile ring's holes at different heights, 60 to 90 mm apart in height reads best. Keep the whole mobile out of a baby's reach: mount it high, keep the cords short, and take it down once the baby can push up on hands and knees. Check knots and cords regularly. Nothing here has been load- or safety-tested.